
  <sn><md>### Continued proportion

By continued proportion of $a, b, c$, it is meant that $a : b = b : c$. 
Here 
- $a, b, c$ will be continued proportion, if and only if $b^2 = ac$. 
- In case of continued proportional, all the quantities are to be of `same kind`. 

In this case, $c$ is called the third proportional of $a$ and $b$, and $b$ is called the `mid-proportional` of $a$ and $c$.
</md></sn>
